From 1703b5c61c9b26b6c76e30ae432c7562e1985bb2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 18:49:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] meta: assign the new catalog to the system user before
 anything reads it

The create works and the very next call fails. ensureVehicleCatalog makes the
catalog on the borrowed admin token, that token is dropped, and
ensureProductFeed runs on the BISU -- which is scoped to the assets the dealer
ticked in the login dialog, and a catalog that did not exist at tick time is
not one of them.

Observed live on the Battle Ground lot, 6 Aug 2026:

  GET /1570055258131864/product_feeds
  400  code 100  subcode 33  GraphMethodException
  "Unsupported get request. Object with ID '1570055258131864' does not exist,
   cannot be loaded due to missing permissions, or does not support this
   operation."
  trace AaUw13Qhw0DZsWLainx4DNb

The object existed -- we had just created it. It is the missing-permissions
arm. Note there is no 1690129 and no code 10, so classify() files it as
'request' and the dealer is told to try again in a moment, which never helps
because nothing about waiting grants a role.

POST /{catalog_id}/assigned_users with MANAGE and ADVERTISE, on the admin
token, while it is still in hand -- it is the only credential in the process
with the business-admin standing that granting a role requires. CREATED only:
an adopted catalog was already assigned to us, which is why we could see it.

Failure is fatal to the lot rather than pressed on with. Continuing would
record a catalog we cannot feed as a success, which is the same shape of bug
this investigation began as.

Also drops "Reconnect with an account that is an admin" from the 1690129
dealer message. It sat directly above the admin-grant button and contradicted
it: the button borrows a sign-in for one call and leaves the system-user
connection untouched, while the words told the dealer to tear it down. On a
2FA business that is a confirmation code spent to make things worse, and it is
what a reader of that box actually tried.

tsc --noEmit --incremental false clean; npm run build clean.

